# TODO - WPA2/CCMP

## Objective

Complete theoretically reviewed PMK/PTK, EAPOL MIC and four-way handshake, AES
unwrap, CCMP, keycache, group rekey and packet-number/replay control. Compare
algorithms with published specifications and source vectors; **do not run test
suites or claim crypto certification**.

## Acceptance

- [ ] Implement/review the stated source and integrate on main.
- [ ] Complete safe nonce, keycache, replay and cryptographic lifecycle contracts.
- [ ] Ground decisions in public code, published standards and SDK/KDK references.
- [ ] Record unresolved assumptions and fail-closed behavior.
- [ ] Complete with source/static evidence, NEVER requiring a physical Dell test.

## Required source deliverables

- [ ] Complete PMK/PTK derivation, nonce generation, EAPOL MIC/replay checks,
      the four-way handshake, AES unwrap and GTK rekey with explicit bounds,
      state transitions, timeouts and key erasure on every failure path.
- [ ] Implement actual CCMP protection/deprotection or verified hardware
      offload, keycache programming/removal and TX/RX packet-number lifetime.
      Handle retransmissions, replay, group traffic and connection epochs.
- [ ] Wire cryptographic callbacks to real implementations and packet/key
      consumers. A codec, callback declaration or handshake state enum alone
      does not implement encrypted packet delivery.
- [ ] Keep the controlled data port closed until the accepted handshake and
      keys are installed. Preserve EAPOL access required by authentication;
      disconnect/reset/sleep cannot retain stale usable keys or reuse a PN.
- [ ] Record static algorithm/specification comparisons and reviewed boundary
      cases without executing prohibited test suites or claiming certification.

## Evidence

- Source commits, reference URLs/version/rights, static review and lint diagnostics.
- Theoretical completeness only; no build, device scan, packet logs or hardware claims.
